module

public import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.ExteriorPower.Basic
public import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.TensorPower.Basic

/-!
# The kernel of the map from a tensor power to an exterior power

Let `A → B` be a ring map, let `M` be a `B`-module and let `n ≥ 1`.  The canonical `A`-linear
map `φ : ⨂[A]^n M → ⋀[B]^n M`, `m₁ ⊗ ⋯ ⊗ mₙ ↦ m₁ ∧ ⋯ ∧ mₙ`, has for kernel the `A`-submodule
generated by the pure tensors `m₁ ⊗ ⋯ ⊗ mₙ` with `mᵢ = b • mⱼ` for some `i ≠ j` and `b ∈ B`,
together with the differences `m₁ ⊗ ⋯ ⊗ b mᵢ ⊗ ⋯ ⊗ mₙ - m₁ ⊗ ⋯ ⊗ b mⱼ ⊗ ⋯ ⊗ mₙ`.

The two families lie in the kernel because an alternating `B`-multilinear map vanishes on a
family two of whose entries are `B`-proportional, and takes the same value on a family whose
`i`-th entry has been scaled by `b` as on one whose `j`-th entry has.  For the converse one notes
that the `n`-fold tensor power over `A` carries, for each slot `i₀`, a `B`-module structure in
which `b` scales the `i₀`-th entry of a pure tensor; the second family says that these `n`
structures agree modulo the span `P` of the two families, and this is what makes `P` a
`B`-submodule.  The quotient `(⨂[A]^n M) ⧸ P` is then a `B`-module in which `m₁ ⊗ ⋯ ⊗ mₙ` depends
alternatingly and `B`-multilinearly on `m₁, …, mₙ`, so the universal property of the exterior
power produces a `B`-linear map `⋀[B]^n M → (⨂[A]^n M) ⧸ P` which composed with `φ` is the
quotient map; hence the kernel of `φ` is contained in `P`.

## Main results

* `exteriorPower.ker_eq_span_of_tprod_eq_ιMulti`: Stacks Tag 0H1C in the corrected form,
  with two `B`-proportional entries in the first family, not merely two equal ones.
* `exteriorPower.ker_eq_span_of_tprod_eq_ιMulti_of_two_lt`: the stated form for `n ≥ 3`,
  with two equal entries in the first family.

## Implementation notes

Both families are phrased through `smulEntry m i b = Function.update m i (b • m i)`, scaling one
entry of a family, whose two composition rules `smulEntry_smulEntry_self` and `smulEntry_comm`
carry all the index bookkeeping of the proof.

The `B`-module structure on `⨂[A]^n M` attached to a slot is `moduleSlot`, obtained by
`Module.compHom` from the algebra map `smulSlot`. This algebra map is induced on tensor powers
by the family of `A`-linear maps which is multiplication by `b` in the slot `i₀` and the identity
elsewhere. The module structure is deliberately not an instance: it depends on the
choice of `i₀`, and its underlying `A`-module structure must stay the standard one.  What the
last section needs of it is only the equation `b • x = smulSlot i₀ b x`, so that is what it
assumes, of an arbitrary `B`-module structure on the tensor power.

That the `A`-span of the two families is stable under `smulSlot i₀ b` — the content of
`smulSlot_mem_span`, and the reason the corrected first family is the right one — is checked one
generator at a time, always with the scalar put into the *first* index of the pair `i ≠ j`
recorded by the generator, where the computation stays inside the same family, and then
transported to the slot `i₀` by the second family, which is available for every pair of distinct
slots.  Being stable, the `A`-span is a `B`-submodule `relSpan`, and the quotient by it receives
the alternating `B`-multilinear map `tprodAlternating`.

Faithfulness of the statement to the source, point by point.  Both hypotheses are used:
`hφ` pins `φ`, and `0 < n` is needed, since for `n = 0` the map is the ring map `A → B`
itself, whose kernel is not generated by the (then empty) two families.  The scalars are
the source's: the tensor power is taken over `A` and the exterior power over `B`, and `φ`
is `A`-linear only, `⋀[B]^n M` being viewed as an `A`-module through `A → B`.  The
canonical map is pinned rather than asserted to exist: the conclusion is proved for every
`A`-linear `φ` with `φ (⨂ᵗ m) = ιMulti B n m`, and there is exactly one such `φ`, because
the pure tensors span `⨂[A]^n M`; concretely `φ` is
`PiTensorProduct.lift ((exteriorPower.ιMulti B n).toMultilinearMap.restrictScalars A)`.
A nondegenerate instance: `A = B = ℤ`, `M = ℤ²`, `n = 2`, where the source is free of rank
`4`, the target free of rank `1`, and the kernel is free of rank `3`, generated by
`e₁ ⊗ e₁`, `e₂ ⊗ e₂` and `e₁ ⊗ e₂ + e₂ ⊗ e₁`.

Two departures from the source's form.

First, the source takes as first family the pure tensors with a *repeated* entry,
`mᵢ = mⱼ`; here the entries are only required to be `B`-proportional, `mᵢ = b • mⱼ`.  For
`n ≥ 3` this changes nothing: `mᵢ = b • mⱼ` exhibits `m₁ ⊗ ⋯ ⊗ mₙ` as a tensor with a
repeated entry into whose `k`-th slot, for some `k ∉ {i, j}`, the scalar `b` has been
moved, and the second family absorbs that move.  For `n = 2` the source's first family is
too small, so the lemma as stated there is false: take `A = ℤ`, `B = ℤ[X]`, `M = B` and
`n = 2`.  Then `⋀²_B B = 0`, so the kernel is all of `B ⊗_ℤ B`, whereas the `ℤ`-linear map
`B ⊗_ℤ B → ℤ/2` sending `f ⊗ g` to the coefficient of `X` in `f g` mod `2` annihilates
every `f ⊗ f` (that coefficient is `2 f₀ f₁`) and every `(g f) ⊗ h - f ⊗ (g h)`, while it
sends `1 ⊗ X` to `1`.  The reason is that the kernel of `⨂[B]^n M → ⋀[B]^n M` is a
`B`-submodule, while the `A`-span of the tensors with a repeated entry is stable under
multiplication by `B` only once there is a third slot to receive the scalar.

Second, the source assumes `n > 1`, and the statement is made for `n ≥ 1`, which is the
exact range in which it holds: for `n = 1` both sides are zero, the map `M → ⋀[B]^1 M`
being injective and the two families being empty for want of a pair `i ≠ j`.

## References

* [Stacks 0H1C](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0H1C)
-/

@[expose] public section

open scoped TensorProduct

open Function PiTensorProduct

namespace exteriorPower

section

variable {A B M : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] [AddCommGroup M]
  [Module A M] [Module B M] [IsScalarTower A B M] {n : ℕ}

/-! ### Scaling one entry of a family -/

/-- The family `m` with its `i`-th entry scaled by `b`. -/
private def smulEntry (m : Fin n → M) (i : Fin n) (b : B) : Fin n → M :=
  Function.update m i (b • m i)

private lemma smulEntry_self (m : Fin n → M) (i : Fin n) (b : B) : smulEntry m i b i = b • m i :=
  Function.update_self ..

private lemma smulEntry_of_ne {i j : Fin n} (h : j ≠ i) (m : Fin n → M) (b : B) :
    smulEntry m i b j = m j :=
  Function.update_of_ne h ..

private lemma smulEntry_one (m : Fin n → M) (i : Fin n) : smulEntry m i (1 : B) = m := by
  rw [smulEntry, one_smul, Function.update_eq_self]

/-- Scaling the `i`-th entry of a family whose `i`-th entry has just been updated. -/
private lemma smulEntry_update (m : Fin n → M) (i : Fin n) (x : M) (b : B) :
    smulEntry (Function.update m i x) i b = Function.update m i (b • x) := by
  rw [smulEntry, Function.update_self, Function.update_idem]

/-- Two scalings of the same entry compose. -/
private lemma smulEntry_smulEntry_self (m : Fin n → M) (i : Fin n) (b c : B) :
    smulEntry (smulEntry m i c) i b = smulEntry m i (b * c) := by
  rw [smulEntry, smulEntry_self, smulEntry, smulEntry, Function.update_idem, mul_smul]

/-- Scalings of two different entries commute. -/
private lemma smulEntry_comm {i j : Fin n} (hij : i ≠ j) (m : Fin n → M) (b c : B) :
    smulEntry (smulEntry m j c) i b = smulEntry (smulEntry m i b) j c := by
  simp only [smulEntry, Function.update_of_ne hij, Function.update_of_ne (Ne.symm hij)]
  exact Function.update_comm (Ne.symm hij) ..

end

section

variable {R M N ι : Type*} [Semiring R] [AddCommMonoid M] [Module R M] [AddCommMonoid N]
  [Module R N]

/-- An alternating map vanishes on a family one of whose entries is a scalar multiple of
another entry of the same family. -/
theorem _root_.AlternatingMap.map_eq_zero_of_eq_smul_self (f : M [⋀^ι]→ₗ[R] N) {m : ι → M}
    {i j : ι} (hij : i ≠ j) (b : R) (h : m i = b • m j) : f m = 0 := by
  classical
  have hm : m = Function.update (Function.update m i (m j)) i (b • m j) := by
    rw [Function.update_idem, ← h, Function.update_eq_self]
  rw [hm, f.map_update_smul, Function.update_idem, f.map_update_self _ hij, smul_zero]

end

section

variable {A B M : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] [AddCommGroup M]
  [Module A M] [Module B M] [IsScalarTower A B M] {n : ℕ}

/-! ### Scaling one slot of a tensor power -/

/-- Multiplication by `b : B` on the `i₀`-th slot of the `n`-fold tensor power of `M` over `A`,
`A`-linear in `b` because `PiTensorProduct.map` is multilinear in the family of maps. -/
private noncomputable def smulSlotₗ (i₀ : Fin n) : B →ₗ[A] Module.End A (⨂[A]^n M) :=
  (mapMultilinear A (fun _ : Fin n ↦ M) (fun _ ↦ M)).toLinearMap (fun _ ↦ LinearMap.id) i₀ ∘ₗ
    (Algebra.lsmul A A M).toLinearMap

private lemma smulSlotₗ_tprod (i₀ : Fin n) (b : B) (m : Fin n → M) :
    smulSlotₗ i₀ b (tprod A m) = tprod A (smulEntry m i₀ b) := by
  simp only [smulSlotₗ, LinearMap.coe_comp, comp_apply, MultilinearMap.toLinearMap_apply,
    mapMultilinear_apply, map_tprod, AlgHom.toLinearMap_apply, smulEntry]
  congr 1
  ext j
  rcases eq_or_ne j i₀ with rfl | hj
  · simp
  · simp [hj]

/-- Multiplication by `b : B` on the `i₀`-th slot, as an `A`-algebra map. -/
private noncomputable def smulSlot (i₀ : Fin n) : B →ₐ[A] Module.End A (⨂[A]^n M) :=
  .ofLinearMap (smulSlotₗ i₀) (by ext m; simp [smulSlotₗ_tprod, smulEntry_one])
    fun b b' ↦ by ext m; simp [smulSlotₗ_tprod, smulEntry_smulEntry_self]

private lemma smulSlot_tprod (i₀ : Fin n) (b : B) (m : Fin n → M) :
    smulSlot i₀ b (tprod A m) = tprod A (smulEntry m i₀ b) := by
  rw [smulSlot, AlgHom.ofLinearMap_apply, smulSlotₗ_tprod]

/-- The `B`-module structure on the `n`-fold tensor power of `M` over `A` in which `b : B` acts
on the `i₀`-th slot.  It extends the `A`-module structure along `A → B`. -/
private noncomputable abbrev moduleSlot (i₀ : Fin n) : Module B (⨂[A]^n M) :=
  Module.compHom _ (smulSlot (A := A) (M := M) i₀).toRingHom

/-! ### The two families of relations -/

variable (A B M n) in
/-- The two families of tensors of Stacks 0H1C: the pure tensors two of whose entries are
`B`-proportional, and the differences of two pure tensors obtained by scaling two different
entries of the same tensor by the same `b : B`. -/
private def relSet : Set (⨂[A]^n M) :=
  {x | ∃ (m : Fin n → M) (i j : Fin n) (b : B), i ≠ j ∧ m i = b • m j ∧ tprod A m = x} ∪
    {x | ∃ (m : Fin n → M) (i j : Fin n) (b : B), i ≠ j ∧
        tprod A (smulEntry m i b) - tprod A (smulEntry m j b) = x}

omit [Algebra A B] [IsScalarTower A B M] in
private lemma mem_relSet {x : ⨂[A]^n M} : x ∈ relSet A B M n ↔
    (∃ (m : Fin n → M) (i j : Fin n) (b : B), i ≠ j ∧ m i = b • m j ∧ tprod A m = x) ∨
      ∃ (m : Fin n → M) (i j : Fin n) (b : B), i ≠ j ∧
        tprod A (smulEntry m i b) - tprod A (smulEntry m j b) = x :=
  Iff.rfl

omit [Algebra A B] [IsScalarTower A B M] in
private lemma tprod_mem_span_relSet {m : Fin n → M} {i j : Fin n} (hij : i ≠ j) (b : B)
    (h : m i = b • m j) : tprod A m ∈ Submodule.span A (relSet A B M n) :=
  Submodule.subset_span (Or.inl ⟨m, i, j, b, hij, h, rfl⟩)

omit [Algebra A B] [IsScalarTower A B M] in
private lemma sub_mem_span_relSet (m : Fin n → M) {i j : Fin n} (hij : i ≠ j) (b : B) :
    tprod A (smulEntry m i b) - tprod A (smulEntry m j b) ∈
      Submodule.span A (relSet A B M n) :=
  Submodule.subset_span (Or.inr ⟨m, i, j, b, hij, rfl⟩)

/-- Two slots carry the same action of `b : B` modulo the relations. -/
private lemma smulSlot_sub_mem_span {i₀ k : Fin n} (hik : i₀ ≠ k) (b : B) (x : ⨂[A]^n M) :
    smulSlot i₀ b x - smulSlot k b x ∈ Submodule.span A (relSet A B M n) := by
  have h : (⊤ : Submodule A (⨂[A]^n M)) ≤
      Submodule.comap (smulSlot i₀ b - smulSlot k b) (Submodule.span A (relSet A B M n)) := by
    rw [← PiTensorProduct.span_tprod_eq_top, Submodule.span_le]
    rintro y ⟨m, rfl⟩
    simp only [SetLike.mem_coe, Submodule.mem_comap, LinearMap.sub_apply, smulSlot_tprod]
    exact sub_mem_span_relSet m hik b
  exact h Submodule.mem_top

/-- Membership in the span of the relations does not depend on the slot the scalar is put in. -/
private lemma smulSlot_mem_span_of_slot {i₀ k : Fin n} (b : B) {x : ⨂[A]^n M}
    (h : smulSlot k b x ∈ Submodule.span A (relSet A B M n)) :
    smulSlot i₀ b x ∈ Submodule.span A (relSet A B M n) := by
  by_cases hik : i₀ = k
  · subst hik; exact h
  · simpa using Submodule.add_mem _ (smulSlot_sub_mem_span hik b x) h

/-- The `A`-span of the relations is stable under scaling any slot by any `b : B`.  This is the
heart of the matter: it is what makes that span a `B`-submodule, and hence the quotient by it a
`B`-module. -/
private lemma smulSlot_mem_span (i₀ : Fin n) (b : B) {x : ⨂[A]^n M}
    (hx : x ∈ Submodule.span A (relSet A B M n)) :
    smulSlot i₀ b x ∈ Submodule.span A (relSet A B M n) := by
  induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem y hy =>
      -- In both cases put `b` into the slot `i`, the first of the pair the generator records:
      -- there the scaled generator is again a generator of the same family.
      obtain (⟨m, i, j, c, hij, hm, rfl⟩ | ⟨m, i, j, c, hij, rfl⟩) := mem_relSet.mp hy
      · refine smulSlot_mem_span_of_slot (k := i) b ?_
        rw [smulSlot_tprod]
        refine tprod_mem_span_relSet hij (b * c) ?_
        rw [smulEntry_self, smulEntry_of_ne (Ne.symm hij), hm, mul_smul]
      · refine smulSlot_mem_span_of_slot (k := i) b ?_
        rw [map_sub, smulSlot_tprod, smulSlot_tprod, smulEntry_smulEntry_self, mul_comm,
          ← smulEntry_smulEntry_self, smulEntry_comm hij]
        exact sub_mem_span_relSet _ hij c
  | zero => simp
  | add y z _ _ hy hz => rw [map_add]; exact Submodule.add_mem _ hy hz
  | smul a y _ hy => rw [map_smul]; exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ hy

/-- Both families of relations are killed by the canonical map to the exterior power. -/
private lemma span_relSet_le_ker (φ : (⨂[A]^n M) →ₗ[A] ⋀[B]^n M)
    (hφ : ∀ m : Fin n → M, φ (tprod A m) = exteriorPower.ιMulti B n m) :
    Submodule.span A (relSet A B M n) ≤ LinearMap.ker φ := by
  rw [Submodule.span_le]
  intro x hx
  obtain (⟨m, i, j, b, hij, hm, rfl⟩ | ⟨m, i, j, b, hij, rfl⟩) := mem_relSet.mp hx
  · simp only [SetLike.mem_coe, LinearMap.mem_ker, hφ]
    exact (exteriorPower.ιMulti B n).map_eq_zero_of_eq_smul_self hij b hm
  · simp [hφ, smulEntry]

/-! ### Inverting the map modulo the relations -/

section

variable [Module B (⨂[A]^n M)]

/-- The `A`-span of the relations, as a `B`-submodule for a `B`-module structure scaling the slot
`i₀`.  Its carrier is `Submodule.span A (relSet A B M n)`; that this is a submodule for the
larger ring is `smulSlot_mem_span`. -/
private def relSpan {i₀ : Fin n} (hsmul : ∀ (b : B) (x : ⨂[A]^n M), b • x = smulSlot i₀ b x) :
    Submodule B (⨂[A]^n M) where
  toAddSubmonoid := (Submodule.span A (relSet A B M n)).toAddSubmonoid
  smul_mem' := by
    intro b x hx
    rw [hsmul]
    exact smulSlot_mem_span i₀ b hx

private lemma mem_relSpan {i₀ : Fin n}
    {hsmul : ∀ (b : B) (x : ⨂[A]^n M), b • x = smulSlot i₀ b x} {x : ⨂[A]^n M} :
    x ∈ relSpan hsmul ↔ x ∈ Submodule.span A (relSet A B M n) := Iff.rfl

/-- Modulo the relations, the pure tensor `m₁ ⊗ ⋯ ⊗ mₙ` is an alternating `B`-multilinear
function of `m₁, …, mₙ`: it is alternating by the first family, and a scalar of `B` may be moved
from the slot it acts on to any other slot by the second one. -/
private noncomputable def tprodAlternating {i₀ : Fin n}
    (hsmul : ∀ (b : B) (x : ⨂[A]^n M), b • x = smulSlot i₀ b x) :
    M [⋀^Fin n]→ₗ[B] ((⨂[A]^n M) ⧸ relSpan hsmul) where
  toFun m := (relSpan hsmul).mkQ (tprod A m)
  map_update_add' m i x y := by rw [MultilinearMap.map_update_add, map_add]
  map_update_smul' m i b x := by
    -- The `DecidableEq (Fin n)` bound by the field is not the instance `smulEntry` uses.
    obtain rfl : ‹DecidableEq (Fin n)› = instDecidableEqFin n := Subsingleton.elim _ _
    rw [← map_smul, hsmul, smulSlot_tprod]
    by_cases hi : i = i₀
    · rw [hi, smulEntry_update]
    · rw [Submodule.mkQ_apply, Submodule.mkQ_apply, Submodule.Quotient.eq, mem_relSpan,
        ← smulEntry_update]
      exact sub_mem_span_relSet _ hi b
  map_eq_zero_of_eq' m i j h hij := by
    rw [Submodule.mkQ_apply, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero, mem_relSpan]
    exact tprod_mem_span_relSet hij 1 (by rw [one_smul]; exact h)

private lemma tprodAlternating_apply {i₀ : Fin n}
    (hsmul : ∀ (b : B) (x : ⨂[A]^n M), b • x = smulSlot i₀ b x) (m : Fin n → M) :
    tprodAlternating hsmul m = (relSpan hsmul).mkQ (tprod A m) := rfl

/-- The reverse inclusion, for an arbitrary `B`-module structure scaling the slot `i₀`: the
universal property of the exterior power turns `tprodAlternating` into a `B`-linear map
`⋀[B]^n M → (⨂[A]^n M) ⧸ relSpan hsmul` which composed with `φ` is the quotient map, so the
kernel of `φ` is contained in that of the quotient map. -/
private lemma ker_le_span_relSet_of_smul [IsScalarTower A B (⨂[A]^n M)] {i₀ : Fin n}
    (hsmul : ∀ (b : B) (x : ⨂[A]^n M), b • x = smulSlot i₀ b x)
    (φ : (⨂[A]^n M) →ₗ[A] ⋀[B]^n M)
    (hφ : ∀ m : Fin n → M, φ (tprod A m) = exteriorPower.ιMulti B n m) :
    LinearMap.ker φ ≤ Submodule.span A (relSet A B M n) := by
  have key : (exteriorPower.alternatingMapLinearEquiv (tprodAlternating hsmul)).restrictScalars A
      ∘ₗ φ = (relSpan hsmul).mkQ.restrictScalars A := by
    ext m; simp [hφ, tprodAlternating_apply]
  intro x hx
  have h := LinearMap.congr_fun key x
  simp only [LinearMap.coe_comp, comp_apply, LinearMap.coe_restrictScalars] at h
  have hx0 : (relSpan hsmul).mkQ x = 0 := by rw [← h, LinearMap.mem_ker.mp hx, map_zero]
  rwa [Submodule.mkQ_apply, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero, mem_relSpan] at hx0

end

/-- The reverse inclusion.  Let `B` act on the tensor power through its first slot, which exists
because `n ≥ 1`. -/
private lemma ker_le_span_relSet (hn : 0 < n) (φ : (⨂[A]^n M) →ₗ[A] ⋀[B]^n M)
    (hφ : ∀ m : Fin n → M, φ (tprod A m) = exteriorPower.ιMulti B n m) :
    LinearMap.ker φ ≤ Submodule.span A (relSet A B M n) := by
  let : Module B (⨂[A]^n M) := moduleSlot ⟨0, hn⟩
  have hsmul : ∀ (b : B) (x : ⨂[A]^n M), b • x = smulSlot (⟨0, hn⟩ : Fin n) b x := fun _ _ ↦ rfl
  have : IsScalarTower A B (⨂[A]^n M) :=
    ⟨fun a b x ↦ by rw [hsmul, hsmul, map_smul, LinearMap.smul_apply]⟩
  exact ker_le_span_relSet_of_smul hsmul φ hφ

end

end exteriorPower

/-- **Stacks 0H1C.** Let `A → B` be a ring map, let `M` be a `B`-module and let `n ≥ 1`.
The kernel of the canonical `A`-linear map `M ⊗_A ⋯ ⊗_A M → ⋀[B]^n M`,
`m₁ ⊗ ⋯ ⊗ mₙ ↦ m₁ ∧ ⋯ ∧ mₙ`, is generated as an `A`-module by the pure tensors
`m₁ ⊗ ⋯ ⊗ mₙ` with `mᵢ = b • mⱼ` for some `i ≠ j` and `b ∈ B`, together with the
differences `m₁ ⊗ ⋯ ⊗ b mᵢ ⊗ ⋯ ⊗ mₙ - m₁ ⊗ ⋯ ⊗ b mⱼ ⊗ ⋯ ⊗ mₙ` for `i ≠ j` and `b ∈ B`. -/
@[stacks 0H1C "first family `mᵢ = b • mⱼ`, not `mᵢ = mⱼ`: the latter fails for `n = 2`"]
theorem exteriorPower.ker_eq_span_of_tprod_eq_ιMulti
    {A B M : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] [AddCommGroup M]
    [Module A M] [Module B M] [IsScalarTower A B M] {n : ℕ} (hn : 0 < n)
    (φ : (⨂[A]^n M) →ₗ[A] ⋀[B]^n M)
    (hφ : ∀ m : Fin n → M, φ (PiTensorProduct.tprod A m) = exteriorPower.ιMulti B n m) :
    LinearMap.ker φ =
      Submodule.span A
        ({x | ∃ (m : Fin n → M) (i j : Fin n) (b : B), i ≠ j ∧ m i = b • m j ∧
              PiTensorProduct.tprod A m = x} ∪
          {x | ∃ (m : Fin n → M) (i j : Fin n) (b : B), i ≠ j ∧
              PiTensorProduct.tprod A (Function.update m i (b • m i)) -
                PiTensorProduct.tprod A (Function.update m j (b • m j)) = x}) := by
  have h := le_antisymm (ker_le_span_relSet hn φ hφ) (span_relSet_le_ker φ hφ)
  unfold relSet smulEntry at h
  exact h

/-- For `2 < n` the tensors with two equal entries, together with the scaling differences,
already generate the kernel. -/
@[stacks 0H1C "the stated form, for `n ≥ 3`"]
theorem exteriorPower.ker_eq_span_of_tprod_eq_ιMulti_of_two_lt
    {A B M : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] [AddCommGroup M]
    [Module A M] [Module B M] [IsScalarTower A B M] {n : ℕ} (hn : 2 < n)
    (φ : (⨂[A]^n M) →ₗ[A] ⋀[B]^n M)
    (hφ : ∀ m : Fin n → M, φ (tprod A m) = exteriorPower.ιMulti B n m) :
    LinearMap.ker φ =
      Submodule.span A
        ({x | ∃ (m : Fin n → M) (i j : Fin n), i ≠ j ∧ m i = m j ∧ tprod A m = x} ∪
          {x | ∃ (m : Fin n → M) (i j : Fin n) (b : B), i ≠ j ∧
              tprod A (update m i (b • m i)) - tprod A (update m j (b • m j)) = x}) := by
  rw [exteriorPower.ker_eq_span_of_tprod_eq_ιMulti (by omega) φ hφ]
  refine le_antisymm ?_ (Submodule.span_mono ?_)
  · rw [Submodule.span_le]
    rintro x (⟨m, i, j, b, hij, hm, rfl⟩ | hx)
    · obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ : ∃ k : Fin n, k ∉ ({i, j} : Finset (Fin n)) := by
        by_contra! h
        have h₁ := Finset.card_le_card (fun k _ ↦ h k : (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin n)) ⊆ {i, j})
        have h₂ := Finset.card_le_two (a := i) (b := j)
        rw [Finset.card_univ, Fintype.card_fin] at h₁
        omega
      simp only [Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton, not_or] at hk
      -- `m` is `m'` with its `i`-th entry scaled by `b`, where `m' i = m' j`;
      -- move `b` to slot `k`.
      set m' := update m i (m j) with hm'
      have hm'i : m' i = m j := update_self ..
      have hm'j : m' j = m j := update_of_ne (Ne.symm hij) ..
      have hmm' : m = update m' i (b • m' i) := by
        rw [hm'i, hm', update_idem, ← hm, update_eq_self]
      rw [SetLike.mem_coe, hmm', ← sub_add_cancel (tprod A (update m' i (b • m' i)))
        (tprod A (update m' k (b • m' k)))]
      refine Submodule.add_mem _
        (Submodule.mem_span_of_mem (Set.mem_union_right _
          (Set.mem_ofPred.mpr ⟨m', i, k, b, Ne.symm hk.1, rfl⟩)))
        (Submodule.mem_span_of_mem (Set.mem_union_left _
          (Set.mem_ofPred.mpr ⟨update m' k (b • m' k), i, j, hij, ?_, rfl⟩)))
      rw [update_of_ne (Ne.symm hk.1), update_of_ne (Ne.symm hk.2), hm'i, hm'j]
    · exact Submodule.mem_span_of_mem (Set.mem_union_right _ hx)
  · rintro x (⟨m, i, j, hij, hm, rfl⟩ | hx)
    · exact Set.mem_union_left _ (Set.mem_ofPred.mpr ⟨m, i, j, 1, hij, by rw [one_smul, hm], rfl⟩)
    · exact Set.mem_union_right _ hx
